{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Diffusion Models \u2014 DDPM from Scratch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements a 1-D DDPM. Data is a two-mode mixture. The \"net\" is a tiny MLP that takes `(x_t, t)` and outputs predicted noise. Training is the one-line loss. Sampling iterates the reverse chain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: the forward schedule (closed form)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "betas = [1e-4 + (0.02 - 1e-4) * t / (T - 1) for t in range(T)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "alphas = [1 - b for b in betas]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "alpha_bars = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "cum = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for a in alphas:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cum *= a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    alpha_bars.append(cum)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: sample `x_t` in one shot"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def forward_sample(x0, t, alpha_bars, rng):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    a_bar = alpha_bars[t]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    eps = rng.gauss(0, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x_t = math.sqrt(a_bar) * x0 + math.sqrt(1 - a_bar) * eps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x_t, eps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: one training step"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_step(x0, model, alpha_bars, rng):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    t = rng.randrange(T)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x_t, eps = forward_sample(x0, t, alpha_bars, rng)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    eps_hat = model_forward(model, x_t, t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = (eps - eps_hat) ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return loss, gradient_step(model, ...)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: reverse sampling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sample(model, alpha_bars, T, rng):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = rng.gauss(0, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for t in range(T - 1, -1, -1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        eps_hat = model_forward(model, x, t)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        beta_t = 1 - alphas[t]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = (x - beta_t / math.sqrt(1 - alpha_bars[t]) * eps_hat) / math.sqrt(alphas[t])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if t > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x += math.sqrt(beta_t) * rng.gauss(0, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For a 1-D problem with 40 timesteps and a 24-unit MLP, this learns the two-mode mixture in ~200 epochs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Change T from 40 to 10 in `code/main.py`. How does sample quality (visual histogram of outputs) degrade? At what T does the two-mode structure collapse?\n2. **Medium.** Switch from \u03b5-prediction to v-prediction. Re-derive the reverse step. Compare final sample quality.\n3. **Hard.** Add classifier-free guidance. Condition on a class label `c \u2208 {0, 1}`, drop it 10% of the time during training, and at sampling time use `\u03b5 = (1+w)\u00b7\u03b5_cond - w\u00b7\u03b5_uncond`. Measure the conditional-mode-hit rate at `w = 0, 1, 3, 7`."
      ]
    }
